INT. HALLORAN PLANETARIUM - DOME - NIGHT

The dome overhead is black and bare, the projector asleep in the center of the room like a great iron insect. Rows of tilted seats. A single work lamp on a stand.

Five people, arranged by accident into a rough circle. No one has taken a seat.

PROFESSOR ARISTIDE BOUCHARD, 70, tweed, bow tie, pale from a long illness, cradles a tin of lens cloths. JUNE ASANTE, 20s, his research assistant, a clipboard against her chest. ROBBO DUNN, 50s, caretaker, boiler suit, holds a ring of keys the size of a fist. DETECTIVE MAXWELL CROFT, 40s, trench coat, notebook, unhurried.

And in the center aisle, a WOMAN IN VIOLET, 50s, gloves, veil pushed back, who has not moved since the lights went down.

CROFT
Professor, you reported the break-in at nine.

BOUCHARD
At nine twenty.

CROFT
And the thing that was stolen.

BOUCHARD
A glass plate. A photograph of the sky. Nothing the world would miss.

Robbo looks at his keys. June adjusts her clipboard. The Woman in Violet watches the empty dome.

CROFT
Then why did the alarm trip on all four doors at once?

ROBBO
Old wiring.

CROFT
Is that so.

ROBBO
Old wiring. Aye.

June clears her throat. Everyone looks. She looks away.

CROFT
Miss Asante?

JUNE
The plate was from 1919. It showed the eclipse that proved Einstein.

BOUCHARD
June.

JUNE
It's worth something, Professor.

BOUCHARD
Not to us.

CROFT
To someone.

The Woman in Violet takes one step toward the projector. Robbo takes one step back.

WOMAN IN VIOLET
You've left the lamp on.

ROBBO
Aye, ma'am.

WOMAN IN VIOLET
It spoils the dark.

Robbo reaches for the switch. Hesitates.

CROFT
Leave it.

The Woman in Violet turns. Slowly. Regards the detective with the same calm she brought to the dome.

CROFT (CONT'D)
And you are?

WOMAN IN VIOLET
A friend of the late Mr. Halloran.

BOUCHARD
Cordelia.

The name falls into the room like a coin. June looks at the professor. Robbo looks at the floor.

CORDELIA VANE, as the Woman in Violet is now, smiles faintly.

CORDELIA
Aristide. You look well.

BOUCHARD
I look dying.

CORDELIA
Yes. That too.

She opens her handbag. Takes out a flat object wrapped in black silk. Sets it gently on the arm of a seat. Nobody speaks.

CROFT
Is that what I think it is?

CORDELIA
It is what it always was.

She walks past all of them, out through the dark doorway of the dome. Her heels tick on the marble. Fade. The professor does not look at the plate. He looks at his hands.

JUNE
Professor?

BOUCHARD
Turn the lamp off, Robbo.

Robbo does. The dome goes black. Somewhere overhead, a switch clicks, and a thousand false stars bloom.
